	"data": "Home Assistant — What's Relevant Going Forward\n\nResearch summary for Home Assistant running on pi5 (HA hub). Focus: what matters for cithoreal's setup and the Calcifer integration vision.\n\n🔑 The Biggest Thing: MCP Server (Model Context Protocol)\n\nWhat it is: HA now ships a built-in MCP Server integration. MCP is the open standard that lets AI assistants talk to external tools. Home Assistant exposes its entire Assist API as MCP tools.\n\nWhat this means for Calcifer:\nI can connect to your Home…",
